in the interim it's going to be andy  dalton at quarterback  for the dallas cowboys coach mike  mccarthy talked yesterday  yesterday about his own experience on  having to go with a backup because he's  had to do it a few times in the past  specifically when he was with the  packers he is  well um i think it depends on you know  who  who's who's playing after you lose a  starter i mean  there was moments there in the past that  um you know we we did some good things  with with our back  our backups but there was moments where  we did not so  uh i think the first step is you have to  make sure  everybody in the room is ready and in in  that backup  quarterback is is ready to play so the  offense can continue to grow and move  forward  especially in a year like this where  it's the first year for all of us  you know we've achieved that with andy  dalton so i have great confidence in  in where we are as an offense and you  know we still need to improve on some  things  and you know we'll still be able to do  that uh with with andy playing  quarterback  you know i remember a time when ted  thompson the former gm of the packers  explained that they did not have a  strong backup to aaron rodgers because  and i kid you not they didn't want  to jinx rogers by having  a great backup yeah it made no sense  then  it makes no sense now no and with with  look without him  in 2013 you look at the reduction in  points 29-4 down to 21-7  without him in 2017 for nine games you  see the reduction 24-4 down to 16-6  and again it's this idea chris that  they they really who's ever been the  great backup quarterback  behind aaron rodgers they've just never  had one no they have not  you know that was that was it's risky  especially when  you know you put so much on aaron  rodgers plate to make plays  and kind of like we've always talked  about carry the offense  it's those type of guys that usually  generally get hurt because they have to  you know play on the edge of  recklessness at times to help their team  win and  that's exactly what happened to aaron  rodgers i mean when he broke his  collarbone both times it's he's  scrambling and trying to make something  happen for the team and got caught in  some bad positions but  uh this is why you pay money  for a backup quarterback because no andy  dalton is not dak prescott but he's  still damn good  and their offense is not gonna have to  change  he's still gonna be able to do  physically just about everything dak  prescott can do now he's going to be  able to do on the same level no  he doesn't have as big as an arm he's  not going to be as good in the pocket  with people around him  and and certainly not as good a runner  but he's still a good athlete and can  throw the ball on the run and do  those things to where uh you know again  i don't think  things will have to change not with that  wide receiving core and that was one of  the great offseason  acquisitions by the cowboys the fact  that they had the vision to go you know  what  our team our offense is awesome our  offense might have to carry the team a  little bit  wait let's make sure we have some  insurance in case one guy goes down to  where  everything doesn't fall apart and this  is uh this is that case right here  yeah and uh you're right and look  they're two and three they're in first  place in the division  and i really do believe that these  circumstances  reduce the expectations just enough to  take a lot of the heat off of the  players maybe some of the heat off of  the coaching staff  and they can just take care of business  in the division try to get better and  try to get to the point where  come january if they are hosting a  playoff game they can win that they can  build some  some momentum build some confidence and  then go into the divisional round and  try to do something that they haven't  done since 1995 which is win the game  that puts them in the nfc championship  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure